# 🍽️ LULU — Restaurant Website

A premium one-page website built as a freelance proposal for **LULU Restaurant**, a contemporary restaurant in Abidjan, Côte d'Ivoire.

## 🎯 Project Context

I live right across the street from LULU and noticed they had no real website of their own, only third-party listings on review and reservation platforms. I built a complete demo on my own initiative and presented it directly to the restaurant's team, as a way to pitch real client work while learning web development.

## 🚀 Live Preview

👉 https://emm0546.github.io/lulu-restaurant/

> **Note:** This is a client proposal, not yet the restaurant's official production site. Menu items and some details are placeholders pending real content from the restaurant.

## 🎨 Features

- **Elegant, Premium Design** — Serif display type (Cormorant Garamond) paired with a clean sans-serif body font (Jost), a warm neutral palette, and generous spacing to match the restaurant's upscale positioning.
- **Fully Responsive** — Built with CSS Grid and Flexbox, with a dedicated mobile layout (nav, hero, menu, footer all adapted for small screens).
- **Sticky Navigation** — Header stays accessible while scrolling, with smooth anchor-link scrolling between sections.
- **One-Page Structure** — Hero, L'expérience, La carte (menu), Événements, À propos, Réservation, and Contact, all in a single smooth-scrolling page.
- **Direct Reservation Flow** — A "Réserver sur WhatsApp" button opens a pre-filled WhatsApp message, no booking form or backend needed.
- **Embedded Google Map** — Live, interactive map pointing to the restaurant's real location, plus a direct "Voir sur Google Maps" link.
- **Real Contact Channels** — Phone (`tel:`), WhatsApp (`wa.me`), and email (`mailto:`) links, all wired to the restaurant's actual contact details.
- **Social Links** — Instagram and Facebook, confirmed as the restaurant's real accounts.

## 🛠️ Built With

- **HTML5** — Semantic structure
- **CSS3** — Grid, Flexbox, custom properties, responsive design, animations
- **Google Fonts** — Cormorant Garamond & Jost
- **Google Maps Embed** — No API key required
- **Git & GitHub** — Version control
- **GitHub Pages** — Live hosting for the demo

## 📚 What I Practiced

- Semantic HTML structure for a one-page business site
- CSS Grid & Flexbox for responsive, multi-section layouts
- Mobile-first debugging (nav overflow, footer alignment, iframe sizing)
- Typography and visual hierarchy for a premium brand feel
- Writing clean, de-duplicated, well-organized CSS
- `wa.me`, `tel:`, and `mailto:` link formatting
- Client communication: pitching, following up, and drafting a service contract

## 💼 Status

Currently a proposal under review by the restaurant's owner. If accepted, next steps include:

- Replacing placeholder menu items with the real carte
- Adding real photography (hero image, dishes, interior)
- A signed service agreement covering site delivery and ongoing monthly maintenance

## Future Improvements

- Real menu with categories, descriptions, and pricing in FCFA
- Professional photography throughout
- Possible stock management tooling for the restaurant (separate project, under discussion)
- Moving off GitHub Pages to a dedicated domain and host for production

